  "source_text": "Hecks.bluebook \"Echo\" do\n  # A CORPUS-OWNED DOMAIN (docs/semantics/bluebook-semantics.md, C10.4).\n  # One policy that answers its own command's event with the same command, so a single Ping\n  # starts a chain that never ends on its own. The reaction depth bound is the only thing that\n  # stops it: five reactions below the root run, the sixth is recorded undelivered.\n  vision \"A ping is answered by another ping, until the reaction depth bound says enough.\"\n  core\n\n  aggregate \"Beacon\" do\n    identified_by :name\n\n    attribute :name, Name\n\n    value_object \"Name\" do\n      attribute :value, String\n    end\n\n    command \"Light\" do\n      goal \"Light a beacon\"\n      attribute :name, Name\n      emits \"BeaconLit\"\n    end\n\n    command \"Ping\" do\n      goal \"Ping a beacon, which makes the beacon ping again\"\n      reference_to Beacon\n      emits \"Pinged\"\n    end\n\n    policy \"PingAgain\" do\n      on      \"Pinged\"\n      trigger Beacon::Ping\n    end\n  end\nend\n"
}